# What Memcheck MUST print when tests/bench/leak_canary/main.c is run under
# valgrind with tests/bench/leak.sh's own flags. One substring per line;
# `#` is a comment and a blank line is ignored. EVERY line here has to
# appear in the run's log or leak.sh refuses to gate at all -- see that
# script's header, and main.c's.
#
# It is the REPORT that is asserted, not the exit status. A wrong binary can
# exit non-zero for a dozen reasons that have nothing to do with detection,
# and a right-looking exit 0 is precisely the vacuity this control exists
# to rule out.
